    {
      "id": "inspired-product-s056-p00389",
      "source_en": "Bezos line is very important. So many teams give up on their product vision far too soon. This is usually called a vision pivot, but mostly it’s a sign of a weak product organization. It is never easy, so prepare yourself for that. But, also be careful you don’t get attached to details. It is very possible that you may have to adjust course to reach your desired destination. That’s called a discovery pivot, and there’s nothing wrong with that.",
